    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Print Chinchilla-optimal `(N, D)` for compute budgets `1e20`, `1e22`, `1e24`. Compare to the real model table.\n2. **Medium.** Implement the Hoffmann loss-as-function-of-compute curve. Plot loss vs `log10(C)` for the compute-optimal frontier. Identify when the law predicts we'd need `>10^28` FLOPs for the next 0.1 reduction in cross-entropy.\n3. **Hard.** Fit your own scaling law on 5 tiny models (100K to 10M params) trained on the same dataset. Estimate `\u03b1` and `E`. How well do your exponents match published ones?"
